    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite (a single acceptance test class) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec's \"allow\" behavior already existed in `EnsureUniqueHousehold` (it returns early when `sharesHousehold` is true). The only genuinely new requirement was exposing a **stable, shared `householdId`**.\n\nSince owners in the same household necessarily have identical `lastName`+`address` (any un-flagged duplicate is otherwise rejected with 409), the id can be **derived deterministically** rather than stored and cross-assigned. Two owners in the same household compute the same value automatically \u2014 no DB column, no assignment pipeline step, no schema migration.\n\n**Two files touched:**\n\n1. `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added one `@Transient` derived getter:\n   ```java\n   @Transient\n   public String getHouseholdId() {\n       String key = (this.lastName + \"|\" + this.address).toLowerCase();\n       return String.format(\"H-%08X\", key.hashCode());\n   }\n   ```\n   CC 1, self-contained \u2014 MapStruct picks it up by name (same mechanism as the existing `getInitials()`), so it flows into `OwnerDto` on every GET with no mapper change.\n\n2. `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added `householdId` (readOnly string) to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n**Structural impact kept low:** no existing function was modified \u2014 the one new method has CC 1, and no writes to the large POST pipeline, `EnsureUniqueHousehold`, the mapper, or the SQL schemas were needed.",
